    <string name="i18n_ai_text_correction_explanation">The ✨ button on the toolbar fixes selected text, or all text in the field if nothing is selected. “Auto” tries Gemini Nano on-device first, if available; otherwise it uses the service configured with an API key, then the free LanguageTool checker. Cloud services receive the text being corrected.</string>
    <string name="i18n_language_settings_explanation">Switch languages with the 🌐 button (long-press to open the language list) or swipe on the spacebar. Available languages: {0}. Suggestions use frequency dictionaries: Russian, English, and Chinese are built in; other dictionaries are downloaded (~0.3–0.8 MB). Chinese uses Pinyin (nihao → 你好), Japanese uses Romaji (konnichiha → こんにちは), Korean syllables are assembled automatically, and Vietnamese uses Telex.</string>
    <string name="i18n_layout_editor_explanation">Tap two keys to swap them. Long-press a key to replace it with your own character: a letter, number, or symbol. Long-press variants move with their key.</string>
    <string name="i18n_plugin_help">To install: tap “Import from file” and choose a plugin (.json, .js, or .zip), or copy its text and tap “Import from clipboard.” The plugin will appear in the list below, where you can enable, disable, or delete it.\n\nTo use it: on the keyboard, tap the grid button in the upper left, then 🧩 to open plugin tabs with their buttons and panels. Plugin-pinned buttons appear directly on the toolbar.\n\nTo create your own: save the example using the button below, edit it, and import it. See PLUGINS.md for the format.</string>
    <string name="i18n_custom_icon_help">Tap an icon to replace it with an image (transparent PNGs work best), an emoji, or text. Images can be tinted to match the theme. Plugins can also customize icons.</string>
    <string name="i18n_toolbar_order_help">Controls the order of toolbar buttons (open the toolbar with the grid button in the upper left). You can also reorder buttons on the keyboard itself: long-press a button and drag it left or right.</string>
